course: dictionary
lesson: 5950
title: Masterpiece: a work of great skill
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A masterpiece is a noun for something made with great skill, such as a painting, a book, a piece of music, or anything else that is one of the best of its kind. Use the clues around the word to understand it.
explain: «Every artist learns by copying: tracing a fox from a book, singing a famous song, drawing a cartoon character, or painting a copy of a masterpiece in a gallery.» The sentence says artists copy masterpieces to learn, so a masterpiece must be a work worth copying. Check by swapping in your meaning: "a work of great skill worth copying" still makes sense.
explain: People also use the word playfully. Your friend may say, "My sandwich is a masterpiece!" to mean it is extremely good. The word can also mean the best work a particular person has ever made, so the context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: A masterpiece is a work of art, book, music or other creation of great skill.
fact: A masterpiece is one of the best of its kind.
fact: The best work a particular person has ever made is also called their masterpiece.
fact: You can call anything done extremely well a masterpiece, like a goal or a cake.
fact: Long ago, a craftsman made a masterpiece to prove he was skilled enough to be a master.
exercise: «Every artist learns by copying a masterpiece in a gallery.» What is a masterpiece? | *A work of great skill, one of the best of its kind | A cheap copy made in a rush | A kind of gallery guide | A tool for painting
exercise: Mia says her Lego tower is a masterpiece. What does she mean? | It is the tallest tower in the world | *It is something she has built extremely well | It is a Lego set for sale in shops | It is made of wood
exercise: Long ago, a craftsman made a masterpiece. Why? | *To show he was skilled enough to be a master | To sell it for lots of money in shops | To forget how to make things | To be given a holiday
test: Which of these is a good example of a masterpiece? | A scribbled note on a napkin | *The Mona Lisa, hanging in a gallery | A bent spoon | A crumpled paper bag
test: What is the best work a particular person has ever made called? | *Their masterpiece | Their diary | Their hobby | Their holiday
exam: «Every artist learns by copying a masterpiece in a gallery.» Which clue shows that a masterpiece is worth copying? | Galleries are closed on Mondays | It is a fox from a book | *Artists learn by copying it, so it must be excellent | Artists dislike galleries
